Z||000008||cadaver||07-29-2001||12:40 AM||||So first we have this. <BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>    The I told him I don't like civics but I sure as hell like the vteck si's </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Then we have this.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>   Still hate ricers. I like japanese cars...Vteck civics kick ass! I also love s2000's ,supra's, mr2's and 300z's. The car I race last night was not rice. It was a kick ass racing machine. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No I dont think it was a kick ass race machine. I think it was a street car with some mods. Kick ass race machines are driven on the track by people that know better than to endanger everyone that happens to be on the street that night.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroKyle||07-29-2001||01:12 AM||||Well, you have to have some fun I am ok with street racing if it doesn't get out of hand. Once there is a clear winner ya have to stop (Usually first to 50 to 70 mph does good). No telling when a cop or some idiot gets in the way! Actually, this is my opinion, I don't like the Jap cars. They don't impress me what so ever. Sounds like ya killed the monkey the first race. Good one! The Fiero is way underestimated (the GTs).<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign_1.jpg">  <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>AOL Name: Yakty Yak<BR>E-Mail: YaktyYak@aol.com<P>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||JayUSA77||07-29-2001||02:47 AM||||hey guys, <BR>  I have to agree street racing is dangerous but it depends on your defenition of it.  I do go racing but i would never race on residential streets or on the freeway with civilians around. We take it to the abandoned streets at 2 in the morning and all of us are racers and know the consequences of our actions, when you race on the street any one can be hurt including children and thats not cool.  If your going to race do it responsible. and oh ya if your going to race WIN. <BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||Galen||07-29-2001||07:05 AM||||Forget about the children, what about that elderly old lady that was crossing the street to get to the bar to get hammered... How do you think she would feel about being slammed on by a civic si and being flung like along way across the road? Think before you race, the race  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> thats all I ask<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"And God said there shall be one in thy owns image, and he made me"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.50 Today</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||firstfiero||07-29-2001||11:11 AM||||    If you don't think a civic si is a sports car then our fiero's certanly aren't sports cars. The si is not only faster but will out handle our beloved fiero.<BR>     Why is it every time someone brings up a little street race on this board all of you damn old folgies have to come out and waste threads shaking your finger at us. I don't go above 50 and I only race for a block. It's not like were playing fast and furious out their with nitro and racing down city streets doing 160 mph. Who's being more of danger in my story Me who didn't get any faster then 50 or the ass that was backing up a one way street right down the center lane? At least I was going in the right direction!<BR>    <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000013||Will||07-29-2001||01:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JayUSA77:<BR><B>all of us are racers and know the consequences of our actions</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How does one become "a racer"? Does the SCCA offer a Street Racing Certification now?<P>I'll admit that I race, and probably will more often as my car gets more powerful.<BR>I also agree, don't race stupid. Take every precaution to insure that you're not endangering non-participants.<BR>But just remember that the consequences of your actions could include the death of an uninvolved individual. And you have NO right to risk the life of someone who's not down with being "a racer".||||reg||1
Z||000014||Indiana_resto_guy||07-29-2001||02:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>    Why is it every time someone brings up a little street race on this board all of you damn old folgies have to come out and waste threads shaking your finger at us. I don't go above 50 and I only race for a block. It's not like were playing fast and furious out their with nitro and racing down city streets doing 160 mph. Who's being more of danger in my story Me who didn't get any faster then 50 or the ass that was backing up a one way street right down the center lane? At least I was going in the right direction!<BR>    <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Call me an 'old fogey' if you want, but I call it more of a good use of 'common sense' in knowing that there is a proper place and time to do any racing-street or other wise. City streets? Definitely NOT, too many variables of things that could go wrong! Seldom used country roads? If you must, this takes out the pedestrian and cross traffic variable.<BR>In all actual fact the thread was pointed out by my 20 year old son who said 'look at what this stupid Mother F***er is doing!<BR>Is he an 'old fogey' too? Or does he just have more common sense than you do?<BR>I don't want to start any kind of flame war with anyone on this, I just want to point out the danger that the action brings to the uninvolved combatants in this act!<BR>Sorry if your pi$$ed of with my opinion!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||firstfiero||07-29-2001||05:27 PM||||      Again I ask sir who is more dangerous me or the idiot backing the wrong way up a one way street?<BR>      Things happen every day on the street that are dangerous...I had an *******  today pull out in front of me after looking rite at me and seeing me coming causing me to come to a screeching stop! Their is danger every time you walk out your door. Block to block racing isn't anymore dangerous then driving down the street. <BR>      All I can say about your son being 20 and thinking like you is does he have sense or lack balls. If he think it's a bad thing that's fine...don't do it. I won't point my finger at him and call him a wuss for not racing....so don't point a finger at me and call me dangerous for having a little fun.<BR>     by the way...Flame away...I got thick skin. <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Tryxalon||07-29-2001||06:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> Again I ask sir who is more dangerous me or the idiot backing the wrong way up a one way street? - FirstFiero <HR></BLOCKQUOTE> <P>Well, in my opinion, both of you are dangerous idiots.<P>However, my experience teaches me that stupidity is a self-correcting sin. Either you will finally do something so stupid that the near death experience "wakes you up", or you do something stupid enough to remove yourself from the gene pool.  <P>That is why I smile and laugh at "street racers" and other "exhibitions of lack of survival skill".  Natural selection, ya know. <P>:lol :evil <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000017||Standard||07-29-2001||11:09 PM||||Just a comment on the sport car thing... the civic is <B>not</B> a sports car.  It's a sport coupe.  Sports cars don't have back seats  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Look it up in the dictionary  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Indiana_resto_guy||07-30-2001||12:10 AM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>      Again I ask sir who is more dangerous me or the idiot backing the wrong way up a one way street?<P>I say:<BR>Reality dictates me to say BOTH!<P>      Things happen every day on the street that are dangerous...I had an *******  today pull out in front of me after looking rite at me and seeing me coming causing me to come to a screeching stop!<P>I think you answered your own question here on this one. You are very correct, things DO happen on a daily basis, why make things more dangerous than they already are?<P><BR> Their is danger every time you walk out your door. Block to block racing isn't anymore dangerous then driving down the street. <P>I say:<BR>Again you answered your own question. let me break it down for you in terms.<BR>Your 'Block racing and as stated by FieroKyle "Usually first to 50 to 70 mph does good). No telling when a cop or some idiot gets in the way!" then follow that with your own statement 'I had an *******  today pull out in front of me after looking rite at me and seeing me coming'. <BR>So while 'Block' racing do you think that you can still 'come to a screeching stop!'? <BR>Who gets hurt here? You? Them? Both? The people who are participating? Everyone? No one? Makes me wonder.<P>      All I can say about your son being 20 and thinking like you is does he have sense or lack balls. If he think it's a bad thing that's fine...don't do it. I won't point my finger at him and call him a wuss for not racing....so don't point a finger at me and call me dangerous for having a little fun.<BR>     by the way...Flame away...I got thick skin. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Just a word on my sons ride-'88 Camaro 350 350 horse with a 5-speed manual trans behind it. He also stands near 6' and weighs 210 and knows how to throw it around rather well.<P>I don't think I would build and then give you something like that when you graduate high school due to your lack of common sense and moral responsibility.<P>So far as your 'fun' goes, it has a place to be done, the street, or block, isn't it!<BR>You will realize this sooner or later and I hope it's sooner before you or a friend of yours gets hurt or worse.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 07-30-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 07-30-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||JayUSA77||07-30-2001||12:25 AM||||i think that now a days there is always going to be people that wont race and believe highly against it, the ones who race on occasion but try not to because of the dangers, and the ones who race every thing in site.  I dont think that some of these people can get along because there beliefs are too different but i have racing blood in me. (figure of speech ofcourse) I love to see a car and put the pedal down to the floor and see whos car is better, faster. Im building my car so when i win i know i built it to win. I HATE TO LOSE. and although i race as safe as possible I KNOW there is dangers and thats why i dont do it on city streets.  the people out there that dont race i respect you because your trying to be safe, BUT FACE IT nomatter how good you drive there will always be a dumb sh!t out there not looking and "bamb" he hits you.  and does it matter in the end. At least i know where i drive fast and where not too. I have NO ACCIDENTS on my record so im in good shape. and oh ya someone asked how you get the name as a racer, come to milpitas CA and look for a 86 Fiero GT and ill show you what a racer is and ill show you the reality version of fast and the furious.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
