Z||000023||AusFiero||07-30-2001||09:11 AM||||I was just looking for a picture that might discourage street racing. Couldn't find it unfortunately. But here was the scenario. Subaru WRX turbo racing another car. Drunk steps out onto the road. Subaru trys to miss him. Doesn't. Drunk gets flung 100 metres down the road and killed instantly. Subaru loses control and smashes into several parked car before rolling and going through the front windows of a nightclub where 40 people ended up with injuries. All passengers in the Subaru died and the driver survivies. <P>Now was that a smart thing to do when we can all pay to go use a race track? Plus who would want that on the conscious. <P>Yes even I like to give my car a bit of blast at the lights. But I only take it to the speed limit and definately don't do it where pedestrians are around. If the other car goes flying by then...so what..I know I had won anyway.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000024||FieroGTguy||07-30-2001||09:40 AM||||Here is what I do, which is a nice compromise...<P>1)  Stopped at a red light<BR>2)  A competitive vehicle is next to you<BR>3)  Scan the road (abort if there is traffic &lt;i.e. people trying to beat the red&gt; )<BR>4)  Coast is clear of crossing traffic, no women/children/drunks/mobile creatures/kittens/cops in site.  (excuse the order...  Cops are real @sses around here and I don't like cats!)  hehe<BR>5)  Race to the speed limit.  <P>Fiero's keep the advantage, and no risk of hefty tickets.  Plus, since you are most likely ahead  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, the guy will see your brake lights as their (V-TEC) kicks in.  Rob them of their ego!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Greg  &lt;=  Delivery driver of 4+ years on heavily patrolled Purdue Campus.  Never been pulled over for racing to the speed limit.  Funny as hell when the other guy keeps the race going to prove he can get pulled over first.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>**NOTE:  I deliver until 4am.  No pedestrians, and minimal risk from provoking the other guy.  The opponent almost always slows down after I do because locals know of the risk of speeding on these WELL patrolled streets.**||||reg||1
Z||000025||firstfiero||07-30-2001||10:49 AM||||       Just for the record I'm not a street racer per say. I don't spend all night driving up and down the circuit looking for a race. I was on my way home from work saw this si and just wanted to see if their as quick as they say. I get somebody pulling up to me every night reving their engine. More times then not I do what an earlier poster said. I come off the line fast but then cut it off at the speed limit. You win almost every time that way...not many cars hook up as well as the fiero. add that most kids like to screech their tires...and it makes for a quick race. In fact last week when I had a little race with a vw vr6 was the first time I probobly did anything in months.<BR>      By the way I couldnt' give two shits that your son wighs 210 and is 6 ft. Was that supposed to be some kind of threat? Hold on while I change my under wear....I think I just pissed myself...laughing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||Indiana_resto_guy||07-30-2001||10:57 AM||||<BR>      By the way I couldnt' give two shits that your son wighs 210 and is 6 ft. Was that supposed to be some kind of threat? Hold on while I change my under wear....I think I just pissed myself...laughing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>[/B][/QUOTE]<P><BR>Just to let you know that he's not suffering in the area of 'lacking balls' as you put it.<P>Enuf said.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000027||ferg||07-30-2001||11:39 AM||||Greg &lt;= Delivery driver of 4+ years on heavily patrolled Purdue Campus. Never been pulled over for racing to the speed limit. Funny as hell when the other guy keeps the race going to prove he can get pulled over first. <P>Were you racing when you were delivering pies? If so, then you should know by now that pizza drivers almost never get pulled over.<P>Even if you aren't formally racing, everyone else does when coming around the curve on Northwestern - Remember the guy who flipped his car in front of Einstein's???<P>Well Patrolled streets???? The only thing the cops are after is getting the drunks out of Harry's and stopping the fights at the Boiler Room.<P>I know what you were saying about street racing. Just had to give you a jab since you live down there. When I was down there, a few friends of mine drove for Papa John's- they told me if they had the sign on their car, they could do whatever they wanted. And they did. If you don't deliver pizza's- I apologize.||||reg||1
