Z||000035||FieroGTguy||07-30-2001||04:07 PM||||Sorry...  4+ years delivering unmarked Jimmy John's...  Subs So Fast You'll Freak!  hehe<P>I guess you can call me Ed.  (if you've heard or seen the ads)<P>Btw, I blew away a Papa John's driver last night.  No V-Tec, but they know how to shift for max speed.  (We make enough money to replace cars after they blow up)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000036||FieroGTguy||07-30-2001||04:18 PM||||"Well Patrolled streets???? The only thing the cops are after is getting the drunks out of Harry's and stopping the fights at the Boiler Room."<P>Delivering at the times that I do, you will get pulled over for anything in their pursuit for drunk drivers.<P>I'm not sure if you have been on campus here lately, but the car to cop ratio is higher than anywhere else (probably in the world)  :P<P>Every delivery, I see a car pulled over.  <BR>We Have Approx:<BR>- 6 Purdue University Patrol Cars<BR>- 12 West Lafayette Police cars<BR>- 3 County Sheriff Cars<BR>- 3-5 State Troopers<BR>- And several unmarked cars that I can't make an accurate guess<P>All patrolling a 5 miles radius, and those numbers increase dramatically on the weekends, and double again on game days or major events/holidays.<P>But, they are all very kind when they find out you are feeding the hungry.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I have about 15 warnings in my career.  (mostly drunk checks)  Never for speeding/racing.  As a delivery driver, we pretty much have imunity from "No Turn On Red" signs and the freedom to park wherever you want.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000037||Indiana_resto_guy||07-30-2001||04:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>   what don't you understand about what I said? your link is two knuckleheads going over 100 mph. I didn't and have never come close to those kind of speeds a city streets!! They deserve exactly what they got. I think that fastest I ever got on city streets is maybe 50. most of my races don't get past 40 or so. Yes I have done over 100 on the highway.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OH, I understand perfectly what you said!<BR>What is it that you seem to be unable to grasp in what myself and others are trying to clue you in on? I would much rather see you be among the free and living instead of the alternatives! <BR>Yes, even after this discussion!<P>Do you mean to say when your going 50 MPH on a city street where the limit may be 30 or 35?<BR>I don't know about where you live, around here anything over 15 mph over the limit is reckless driving resulting in a 6 month suspension. <BR>Not to mention what it will do to insurance rates.<P>Well then, I guess that your last sentence may well apply, that one came OFF the freeway!<P>There is also another link further down you may want to check out as well.<P><BR>||||reg||1
