Z||000040||Indiana_resto_guy||07-30-2001||10:02 PM||||It's your life I guess.<P>Who said anything about loosing your license? That happens after repeat offenders that prove they can't obey the law and/or can't drive.<P>It's not just my opinion, it's AGAINST THE LAW, so I must have one hell of a following!<BR>So far as the risk, what gives you the right to choose the risk for other people on the street? <P>Just hope the life you MAY take is your own an not your friends/GF's or someone else's who isn't involved and deserves to live a bit longer.<BR>OR mine, even though it's been tried once already.<P>Get over it? Let's hope YOU don't have to get over it.<P>Yea, I sort of adamant about it, I had a cousin and her 8 year old son struck and killed in OK this year by some 'street racer' while waiting for the school bus. He had NO right to put either of them at risk for his 'fun'.<P>No I'm not comparing you or stereotyping either, just pointing out the possibilities.<BR>Don't go around thinking that it 'will never happen to me', it CAN and sometimes does!||||reg||1
